  _lines:
  - _speakerName: Tablet I
    _dialogueText: Beneath the roots of the world, it stirred.
  - _speakerName: Tablet I
    _dialogueText: The ancient worm slept for ages beyond count, feeding on stone
      and silence. The earth itself bent around its endless body, and those who heard
      its distant rumble called it a god.
